ight y≈480).\n\nSo: Section Title instance at (16,430) in 01 renders at ~470?? Unless I mis-set y. Or... the Watchlist head frame I created contains title+plus in an auto-layout that stretches full width, and I placed... hmm.\n\nHold on. Let me reconsider: maybe the rows shifted UP by 40px, not titles down. Row 5 center: expected 683; if rows shifted up 40, row5 center = 643. In image, DAN row: I see 4 big logos in watchlist area at y≈480, 531, 582, 633, 684 — five logos! (orange DHDI, red AMRI, blue ODD, red PYQ, orange DAN). Centers ≈ 480, 531, 582, 633, 684. Spacing 51. Expected centers: 483, 533, 583, 633, 683. ✓ CORRECT. So rows are correctly placed, and \"Watchlist Saya\" title is at ~478 overlapping row 1. Title should be at 430-454 (title frame 430, text height ~20 → center ~442). Rendered at ~478?? That's +40px.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I'm misreading. Maybe the Watchlist head frame in 01 was placed at (16,470)? Did I make an error? From summary: \"Watchlist Head (16,430) + plus icon, 5 Stock Rows (16,458+i*50)\". If rows start at 458 and title at 430 with height ~22, there's a 6px gap — fine. But rendered title is at 470-490.\n\nOH WAIT. I bet I know what happened: the Watchlist head is an auto-layout frame whose child texts are fine, but the frame itself... no. Alternatively — the \"Watchlist Saya\" TEXT node inside got moved? Actually the visible artifact: logo OVERLAPS title. The title is partially behind the logo. If title at 430 center 441 and row1 logo center 483, they wouldn't overlap. They DO overlap → title ~470+.\n\nPossibility: when I created the plus icon instance and appended, maybe I repositioned the title frame? Or the title frame has auto-layout with hug and I set y AFTER appending (appendChild null issue — I learned to assign variable first). If x/y set failed silently... can't know without probing.\n\nSimilarly screen 02: Trending head frame at (16,378) renders ~45px lower (~425). And \"Rekomendasi\" title at (16,213) renders at ~225 (+12). Region chips at (16,337) render ~350 (+13). Hmm, inconsistent shifts. Actually Rec cards: expected 237, 3 cards of height H with gap g. In image: cards span ~240-330. Then chips ~345-365. Then head ~420.\n\nWait, maybe the rec cards are 100 tall each (not 84): 237+100=337... chips at 337 would overlap card bottom. Rendered chips at ~350 ≈ 337+13. Hmm.\n\nI think I need to probe the actual node positions rather than guess. Let me run a use_figma probe to dump positions of key nodes in screens 01 and 02.\n\n2. **Trend Card change clipped** (01): card content overflows bottom. Trend Card 10:35 component — check its height/padding. Rendered shows change clipped. Fix: increase card height to ~110 or reduce padding/line heights.\n\nAlso in 02, Rec Cards show ticker chip at TOP (NFLX/META/AMZN green chips), then company name \"Netflix, Inc\" wraps to 2 lines, price, then change clipped? In image: AMZN card shows \"Amazon.c om, Inc\" (wrapped weird mid-word), \"1.001.333\", and change NOT visible (clipped below card edge?). NFLX shows \"2.122.340\" then \"−0,20%\" red pill visible at ~345 — overlapping the Asia chips row! So Rec Card content overflows too, and the red change pill overflows below the card.\n\nSo Rec Card (10:54) also overflows. And company text wraps to 2 lines (\"Meta Platforms\" wrapped, \"Amazon.com, Inc\" wrapped mid-word \"Amazon.c om\") — because card width too narrow (105?) with padding, text box narrow.\n\n3. **Index Cards clipped** (02): IHSG/NIKKEI/SENSEX cards show only name label; value \"7.206,92\" + arrow NOT visible — clipped at bottom? Card spans ~100-160; label at 120; value would be at ~140 — but I don't see values. They're clipped or hidden. Actually looking again: cards ~60 tall, name at top, values cut off below card boundary.\n\nSo Index Card 10:60 also clips its second row.\n\nCommon root cause: components with fixed heights too small for content, OR auto-layout frames with clipsContent=true clipping overflowing children, OR children positioned beyond frame bounds.\n\nWait, actually! Another thought: these components were created with auto-layout and I set explicit sizes at creation time (e.g., Trend Card 100 tall). Then later I FIXED component widths (per summary: \"auto-layout components with hug width: instances created BEFORE a component width-fix keep the old width as a size override\"). The Trend Card content (logo+ticker+price+change) with real line heights might exceed 100. And when content is taller than fixed frame height with counterAxisSizingMode FIXED and clipsContent... auto-layout frames DON'T clip by default? Actually frames have clipsContent property; default for auto-layout frames created via createFrame is... clipsContent defaults to true for regular frames? For auto-layout frames created in UI it's false, but via API createFrame default clipsContent=true I think. If clipsContent=true and children exceed height → clipped. That matches!\n\nAnd Section Title / heads overlapping rows — that's a positioning issue on the SCREEN level, not component level. Need to probe.\n\nHmm wait, one more possibility for the title overlap: maybe I placed the Section Title instances correctly, but the Stock Row instances are HUGE (taller than 50) and shifted? No — logos at correct positions.\n\nActually, hmm, let me look at screen 01 again very carefully at the watchlist area: \"nlist Saya\" — the text is \"Watchlist Saya\" with \"Watc\" hidden behind the logo. The logo is drawn ON TOP. If title at (16,430) and row1 at (16,458), logo inside row1 at x=16..40 (24px), y=475..499. Title text at 16..~120, y≈437-455. No overlap possible. But rendered: title at y≈470-490 (center ~478) overlapping logo center 483. So title IS at ~470.\n\nUnless the row logos are NOT where I think... maybe logos are shifted UP out of their rows? Row texts: \"8.600\" at y≈470 and \"+50 (+0,58%)\" at 486 — for row1 expected price at 458+~15=473ish, change ~489. ✓. So row1 text at correct place, row1 LOGO also at 480 center (correct), and title at 478 (wrong, should be 441).\n\nOK so title misplaced by ~37px. What's at 430+40=470? Hmm, maybe I placed the Watchlist head frame at y=470 in the actual code (summary says 430 but the summary could be wrong, or I placed title frame then the frame's children auto-layout moved?). Whatever — probe and fix.\n\nSimilarly screen 02: what about the \"Rekomendasi\" at ~225 vs expected 213+11=224 center — actually fine! Let me recompute: Section Title frame at (16,213), text 15px → center ~222. Rendered \"Rekomendasi\" at ~222. ✓ FINE.\n\nRegion chips at (16,337): rendered ~350?? Chip height 28 → center 351. Expected center 337+14=351. ✓ FINE! I misjudged.\n\nTrending head at (16,378): height ~24 → center 390. Rendered \"Trending ... 24 jam ... Lihat Semua\" at ~425-430. ✗ WRONG by ~37px. Hmm but wait — is that the head, or is the head fine and what I see is...? In image at y≈420: \"ing\" text + \"24 jam ⌄\" + \"Lihat Semua >\". And ROTI logo overlapping \"Trending\" text. If head were at 378-402, row1 (404) logo center 429 would NOT overlap head text (which ends 396). The rendered overlap means head is at ~415-440. So head misplaced ~+37-40px, same offset as 01's watchlist title (+37). Suspicious — same bug pattern: these two heads both placed ~37-40px too low.\n\nInteresting: both heads might have been placed AFTER appending something, or I used a variable and appendChild order issue. OR — both heads were positioned with y set BEFORE appending to screen (x/y reset to 0,0 on append? no, then they'd be at top-left).\n\nHmm, actually here's a thought: if these heads are auto-layout frames containing the title + right-aligned items, maybe I set position and THEN appended children, and appending children changed... no, y is frame-level.\n\nWhatever — probe actual coordinates and fix directly. Also check trend card/rec card/index card clipping by probing component sizes and fixing heights, then recreate instances (delete+recreate instances after component resize).\n\nWait, actually for the clipping cards, maybe simpler: set clipsContent=false? No — better to make card tall enough. Let me probe first.\n\n4. **Screen 01 trend cards**: change clipped at bottom.\n\nAlso there's ANOTHER oddity in 01: the first Trend Card logo — BRRI logo is a blue square \"BANK BRI\", fine. Logos in trend cards look small (24) centered — fine.\n\nAnd in 02, index cards: values missing. Probe.\n\nAlso 02 head: \"Trending\" title + \"24 jam\" + Chevron_Down + \"Lihat Semua\" + Chevron_Right — rendered shows these but \"Lihat Semua\" has chevron '>' at far right ~x=352. OK.\n\nAlso screen 02 rec card company text \"Amazon.c om, Inc\" — mid-word break, ugly; probably fine once card is wider/taller? Text wrapping mid-word happens when the text box is too narrow for the longest word with default break mode... \"Amazon.com,\" is 11 chars; at font 13 ~ 75px. Card width 105 - padding 24 = 81. Should fit barely. It broke \"Amazon.c\" / \"om, Inc\" — so available width < word width. Card might be ~105 wide with padding 12 → 81px. Word \"Amazon.com,\" at Roboto 13px ≈ 78px. Should fit... but rendered it broke. Maybe padding 16 → 73px. Or font is SemiBold 13 ≈ 82px → breaks. Eh.\n\nPriority: fix the big issues:\nA. 01 Watchlist title position (~470 → 430)\nB. 02 Trending head position (~418 → 378)\nC. Trend Card clipped change (01) — fix component height\nD. Rec Card clipped change + narrow wrap (02) — fix component\nE. Index Card values missing (02) — probe/fix\nF. Check 03-06 screenshots too — likely similar clipping issues in components used there (Amount Option? Key Stat Cell? Method Row? Guide Step was fixed. Payment Row? Stepper? Tooltip in chart?).\n\nPlan: \n1. Probe screens 01/02/03/04/05/06 node positions + component sizes (one use_figma read call).\n2. Fix components (heights) + recreate instances where needed; fix misplaced heads.\n3. Screenshot all 6 again.\n\nLet me write the probe script. Names to dump: for each screen frame (16:2,17:2,18:2,20:2,20:117,21:2), list children with x,y,width,height. Also dump component sizes: 10:35 (Trend Card), 10:54 (Rec Card), 10:60 (Index Card), 10:43 (Stock Row), 8:10 Tab Item?, etc.\n\nProbe code:\n\n```js\nconst out=[];\nconst frames=figma.currentPage.children.filter(n=>['01_Aktivitas','02_Trending','03_Detail_Saham','04_Top_Up_Metode','05_Top_Up_Nominal','06_Top_Up_Pembayaran'].includes(n.name));\nfor(const f of frames){\n  out.push('== '+f.name+' '+f.id);\n  for(const c of f.children){ out.push(`  ${c.name} ${c.id} x=${Math.round(c.x)} y=${Math.round(c.y)} w=${Math.round(c.width)} h=${Math.round(c.height)}`); }\n}\nfor(const id of ['10:35','10:54','10:60','10:43','10:11','10:34','8:69','11:17','11:2','11:28','11:31','11:49','11:50','11:60']){\n  const n=figma.getNodeById(id);\n  if(n) out.push(`COMP ${n.name} ${id} ${Math.round(n.width)}x${Math.round(n.height)} clip=${n.clipsContent!==undefined?n.clipsContent:''}`);\n}\nreturn out.join('\\n');\n```\n\nAlso need internals of Trend Card / Rec Card / Index Card components to see why clipping: dump their children with y positions.\n\nLet me also probe inside: for comp of [10:35,10:54,10:60] dump children recursively 2 levels.\n\nThen decide fixes. Let me do it.\n\nAlso, I should get screenshots of 03-06 in parallel with the probe. Actually do probe first, then screenshot 03-06 (4 calls) — or all in parallel: 1 use_figma probe + 4 get_screenshot. They're independent. Yes, parallel.","signature":"b26fa126a8884099adb7bc27"}],"id":"5a6e1055-0e15-4cd3-91fd-a52d3056b7a0","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a1582c6-6201-4705-96fb-bb880f77176a","uuid":"8d21e20c-b719-445b-b080-6dfc60f50cc1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:22:55.934Z","thinking_duration_ms":116582}
