{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"ALARMING: All 6 screens report MISSING via getNodeById! But screenshots of 16:2/17:2/18:2/20:2 worked! So the screens EXIST (screenshots render them) but getNodeById('16:2') returns null?? That's bizarre. Wait — earlier get_screenshot worked with nodeId 16:2 etc. And use_figma getNodeById('16:2') → null?\n\nHmm, maybe the screens are on a DIFFERENT PAGE and getNodeById works across pages normally... getNodeById should find any node in the file. Unless... the screens were moved to another page? Or the IDs changed?? Screenshot tool worked with these IDs though.\n\nWait — maybe getNodeById is async now? No, it's sync. OR the file has multiple pages and getNodeById works fine... Let me think: maybe the issue is that my probe ran on a different file?! fileKey same. Hmm.\n\nActually — maybe the screens are inside page 5:2 but their IDs are different from what I recorded (16:2 etc. might be ids of something else, and screenshot tool resolved... no, screenshot rendered the right screens).\n\nLet me just list pages and their children. Use figma.root.children → page names/ids, and for page 5:2 list children. That'll reveal actual screen node ids.\n\nAlso findings from components:\n- Header/Home 8:36: 187×48 HUG width (pPrim=AUTO). Title grow=0! Actions at x=44 right after title. FIX: pPrim=FIXED + resize(375,48); Title grow=1 (FILL). But careful: Actions contains Menu x=0, Settings x=44 — gap between icons 20 (24+20=44): Actions is HUG with internal absolute positions? Actions w=68, children at x=0 and 44 — not auto-layout inside (absolute). If Actions becomes... it's fine as long as Actions stays HUG and Title grows.\n- Header/Back 8:43: 127×48 HUG. [Back][Title][Help], pad left 12? pad=0,16,0,12 → left 12? order is padT,padR,padB,padL: 0,16,0,12 → right 16 left 12. Title grow=0 → fix grow=1. resize(375,48), pPrim=FIXED. Hmm — Title centered between Back and Help with grow=1: Title would start after Back. Design: title next to back? In screenshot 04, \"← Top Up\" — title right after back ✓ then help far right ✓. Good with Title grow=1.\n  BUT title vertical centering: Back h=24, Title h=19, Help h=24 → counterAlign CENTER presumably. OK.\n- Header/Detail 8:51: 168×48 HUG, [Back][Actions]. FIX: resize(375,48), pPrim=FIXED, Actions grow=1 (FILL) + Actions.primaryAxisAlignItems... Actions has absolute-positioned children (Plus x0, Share x44, Star x88) — not auto-layout! If Actions FILLs to 375-24-32=319 wide, icons stay at left of Actions (x 0,44,88) → still bunched next to Back. Need icons at right: either convert Actions to auto-layout with gap 20 and primaryAxisAlignItems='MAX', or reposition children x = 319-112=207? But Actions width in component after resize = 319 → set children x: Plus=207? Order: Plus, Share, Star at right edge: Star rightmost at x=319-24=295, Share 251, Plus 207. Hmm but which order? Design: plus, share, star left-to-right. So Plus x=207, Share x=251, Star x=295. Simpler: make Actions auto-layout: Actions.layoutMode='HORIZONTAL', itemSpacing=20, primaryAxisAlignItems='MAX', counterAxisAlignItems='CENTER', then children auto-arranged. Children are instances (icons) — converting frame to AL rearranges them fine.\n  Wait — can I set layoutMode on a plain frame? Yes.\n- Section Title 8:70: 106×19 HUG — fine (title width varies). Instances positioned absolutely — OK.\n- Stock Row 10:43: 152 wide HUG! Names w=1. FIX: pPrim=FIXED, resize(343,50). Then Names FILL → 343-40-100-24(gaps 12*2)=179. Values FIXED 100 → Price/Change right-aligned inside (Price x=61 right-aligned ✓ since Values is... Values children: Price x=61, Change x=29 — right aligned, Values probably an AL with primaryAxisAlignItems='MAX'? or absolute. Values w=100 FIXED/HUG vertical. Price at x=61 w=39 → right edge 100 ✓. Change x=29 w=71 → right edge 100 ✓. So right-aligned already (maybe absolute positions). After width fix, they stay right-aligned ✓. Company 108 wide HUG at x=0,y=20 (absolute in Names? Names is AL vertical probably gap 2: Ticker y0 h18, Company y20). Company HUG w=108 — in a 179-wide Names, no truncation issue... \"PT Duatiga Pertama\" at 12px ≈ 100px ✓ fits.\n- Chart 11:60: 343×219 VERTICAL (pPrim=AUTO hug height), pad 12, gap 4: Plot 319×112 (y12..124), Axis (y128..142), Tooltip (y146..207)! Tooltip is a CHILD of the chart's vertical auto-layout — it's STACKED BELOW the axis, not floating over the plot! That's why the tooltip rendered at bottom-left area (chart y 226 abs + 146 = 372 ✓ matches the gray box at ~372!). FIX: tooltip must float over Plot at the dot. In vertical AL, to position freely: set Tooltip.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE' — then it's positioned relative to the chart frame (x,y absolute within chart). Then set tooltip.x/y. layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE' requires... child of AL frame: set child.layoutPositioning='ABSOLUTE', then child.x/y are relative to frame. Dot abs position within chart: Plot at (12,12); dot at Plot(251,71) → chart coords (263,83); Ring (259,79). Tooltip 100×61 above dot: x=263-50=213, y=83-8-61=14? Gap 8 above dot top (79): y=79-61-8=10. So tooltip at (213,10). Check tooltip right edge 213+100=313 < 331 (343-12) ✓.\n  Also chart height: with tooltip absolute, content = Plot 112 + gap 4 + Axis 14 + pad 24 = 154 ✓ hug gives 154. pPrim AUTO → auto height ✓ (it says 219 now because tooltip 61 in flow; after absolute → 154).\n  Wait, the screen 03 chart: rendered 226..~440?? In screenshot, chart bg ended ~440 (Plot area to ~365, axis labels at 375-390, plus tooltip box 372-408 → total 226+219=445 ✓). After fix: 226..380.\n  BUT also the red text overlapping chips at ~228: that's… tooltip is INSIDE chart (clip=false chart? chart frame clip default true for createFrame — if clip true, tooltip at bottom still inside). The red glyphs at 228 — hmm, could be the Axis labels? No. Could be \"1M 3M\" chips having red text? I see red \"ℛ\" between 1M and 3M, red \"ɡ\" between 3M and 6M?? Might be misrende